    "answer": "oep-ke-keph-pharmacy-051-option-1",
    "explanation": "Taking metformin with or after food reduces the gastrointestinal side effects such as nausea, diarrhoea and abdominal discomfort that are common at the start of therapy. Gradual dose titration also helps tolerability.",
