    "answer": "oep-ke-keph-pharmacy-053-option-1",
    "explanation": "Inhaled corticosteroids can cause oral candidiasis (thrush) and hoarseness. Rinsing the mouth with water and spitting after each use reduces local deposition and the risk of thrush. Inhaled steroids are preventers, used regularly, not relievers.",
