    "answer": "oep-ke-keph-pharmacy-062-option-1",
    "explanation": "Statins can rarely cause myopathy and rhabdomyolysis. Patients should report unexplained muscle pain, tenderness or weakness, especially with dark urine, so creatine kinase can be checked and the statin reviewed. Early reporting prevents serious harm.",
