    "explanation": "WHO and Kenyan guidelines recommend low-osmolarity oral rehydration solution plus zinc for childhood acute diarrhoea to prevent dehydration and reduce the duration and severity of episodes. Antibiotics are reserved for specific causes such as dysentery or cholera.",
