    "answer": "oep-ke-keph-pharmacy-031-option-1",
    "explanation": "A 0.9% w/v solution contains 0.9 g per 100 mL. For 500 mL: 0.9 g x (500/100) = 0.9 x 5 = 4.5 g. Percentage w/v always means grams of solute per 100 mL of solution.",
